      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The exhaustion you feel is real, and it makes the idea of fighting feel utterly pointless. Instead of viewing it as a massive battle against your biology, perhaps you could see it as finding a way to manage the weight you carry. Sometimes, the most powerful act isn't a dramatic fight, but the quiet, deliberate choice to offer yourself a little more grace. Even if the outcome feels predetermined, how you experience the journey matters to *you*.",
      "source": "target",
